      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T09:59:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a pretty inefficient way to insert in a sorted list; it doesn\u0027t matter too much considering the likely size of the list, but still, generally I think you\u0027d want something like (untested):\n\n```\nfinal int searchRes \u003d Collections.binarySearch(responses, response.getMinRemainingTtl(now), Comparator.comparingLong(...));\n// binarySearch returns \"the index of the search key, if it is contained in the list; \n// otherwise, (-(insertion point) - 1)\"\nresponses.add(searchRes \u003e\u003d 0 ? searchRes : (-searchRes - 1), responses);\n```",
      "revId": "ea9ffecd6bc11b3d9a0f79c4c461cb85d02122d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
